### PRJ381 backend smoke tests
# Easiest way to run these: install the VS Code extension "REST Client"
# (humao.rest-client), then click the "Send Request" link above each block.
# (Postman works too, or curl in Git Bash — see README.)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1. Health — should return status ok + db "connected"
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Submit a lead (Request More Information) — expect 201 + an id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "hotspotId": "reception",
  "sessionId": "test-session-001"
}

### 3. Send an analytics event — expect 201 + an id
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "test-session-001",
  "eventType": "hotspot_view",
  "area": "TechnoLab",
  "hotspotId": "technolab_pc",
  "durationMs": 4200
}

### 4. Invalid email — should be rejected with 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 5. Invalid eventType — should be rejected with 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "test-session-001",
  "eventType": "bogus"
}
